From c79d65cf805834f141570e956531106de725b67e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:03:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.2: AI Advisor - friendly SSID + TLS via the
 router's own cert

get_wireless_status now reports the user-facing network names, not the
internal MWL onboarding IDs: it resolves the SDN MAINFH profiles the same
way the GUI does (parse sdn_rl, read apm<idx>_ssid + the auth MODE; never
the PSK) and returns radios{} + networks[]. wlX_ssid dropped from the
get_nvram whitelist too.

The advisor now serves TLS using the ROUTER'S OWN httpd certificate
(/etc/cert.pem + /etc/key.pem via the same mssl layer httpd uses) when one
is loaded, and falls back to plain HTTP when none is - not a separate cert.
The request/response path was moved onto a FILE* (ssl_server_fopen / fdopen
"r+"), mirroring httpd; the TLS path closes the socket fd itself since
mssl_close only frees the SSL object. The arming endpoint emits https:// vs
http:// (and a tls flag) based on cert presence; the GUI notes the scheme
and the self-signed-cert caveat. rmcpd links mssl + openssl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
